        "created_at": "2015-03-08T15:29:20.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>We realized it would probably be easier to know what’s going on if everyone could see the nominations as they are happening.&nbsp; <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slightly_smiling_face.png?v=9\" title=\":slightly_smiling_face:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slightly_smiling_face:\">  (Plus it will eliminate the “Oh, someone probably nominated them” issue.  <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/wink.png?v=9\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\"> ) We’ve created two threads for folks to post nominations in: <a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/public-forumite-nomination-thread-forum-awards-2014-7010\">a thread for nominating forumites</a> and this thread for nominating posts/threads.<br><br>The awards for posts/threads are:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Funniest Thread of the Year</li>\n<li>Best Fan Fiction of the Year</li>\n<li>Best Fan Art of the Year</li>\n<li>Best Player Aid of the Year – A specific item that facilitates gameplay for a GtG game</li>\n<li>Best Forum Activity of the Year – An activity created and run on the forums by the community, including play-by-forum (PBF) games</li>\n</ul>\n<br>If you want to nominate a post/thread, you can either post here with a link and the award you're nominating it for or use <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1xheeWop4_jfcOelIcNUKLBBtDLw-lCgjXtKPub5DQIk/viewform?usp=send_form\">the original form for anonymous nominations</a>. For posts here, a quick blurb explaining why you're nominating it is optional and shouldn't be more than a sentence (to avoid it turning into campaigning). If you want to nominate something that's already been nominated, feel free.\n<p>And feel free to include multiple nominations in each post.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/gtg-forum-award-nominations-2014-5454\">Rules are posted in the original nominations thread</a>.</p>\n<p>We'll be posting the nominations that have already been made anonymously, and we'll continue to post those that come in for the next couple of weeks.</p>",
