        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "We realized it would probably be easier to know what&#39;s going on if everyone could see the nominations as they are happening.&nbsp; :slightly_smiling_face:  (Plus it will eliminate the &quot;Oh, someone probably nominated them&quot; issue.  :wink: ) We&#39;ve created two threads for folks to post nominations in: <a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/public-forumite-nomination-thread-forum-awards-2014-7010\">a thread for nominating forumites</a> and this thread for nominating posts/threads.<br /><br />The awards for posts/threads are:\n<ul><li>Funniest Thread of the Year</li><li>Best Fan Fiction of the Year</li><li>Best Fan Art of the Year</li><li>Best Player Aid of the Year &ndash; A specific item that facilitates gameplay for a GtG game</li><li>Best Forum Activity of the Year &ndash; An activity created and run on the forums by the community, including play-by-forum (PBF) games</li></ul>\n<br />If you want to nominate a post/thread, you can either post here with a link and the award you&#39;re nominating it for or use <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1xheeWop4_jfcOelIcNUKLBBtDLw-lCgjXtKPub5DQIk/viewform?usp=send_form\">the original form for anonymous nominations</a>. For posts here, a quick blurb explaining why you&#39;re nominating it is optional and shouldn&#39;t be more than a sentence (to avoid it turning into campaigning). If you want to nominate something that&#39;s already been nominated, feel free.\n\nAnd feel free to include multiple nominations in each post.\n\n<a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/gtg-forum-award-nominations-2014-5454\">Rules are posted in the original nominations thread</a>.\n\nWe&#39;ll be posting the nominations that have already been made anonymously, and we&#39;ll continue to post those that come in for the next couple of weeks.",
